        "{\"event\":{\"at\":\"2026-11-03T21:13:37.674Z\",\"kind\":\"decision.recorded\",\"payload\":{\"adr\":\"ADR-2\",\"alternatives\":\"Regex `^export\\\\s+` (also tab after export): rejected, the request named the `export ` prefix and a tab-separated form is not a habit worth widening the grammar for; easy to add later in both packages at once. Strip `export` before the comment check: rejected, a commented `# export X=1` must stay a comment. Treat `export NOVALUE` as a key with empty value (shell semantics): rejected, the accessor skips every line without `=` and that stays uniform. Change the PHP package in a later PR: rejected by ADR-1.\",\"rationale\":\"`export KEY=value` is read as `KEY=value`: after the line is trimmed and found not blank or a comment, a leading `export ` is removed and the rest is left-trimmed, so `export   KEY=v` also works. The same code shape is in packages/js/src/accessors/formats/env-accessor.ts and packages/php/src/Formats/EnvAccessor.php (ADR-1). A key that merely starts with the word (`export=1`, `EXPORT_KEY=2`) is unchanged, `export NOVALUE` (no `=`) is still skipped like any line without `=`, and `# export X=1` stays a comment. Tests for these cases are in both packages.\",\"title\":\"EnvAccessor drops only a leading literal `export ` (space), in both packages\"},\"run\":\"01a1a342-6b70-7000-998a-a2ec37b9bd73\",\"signerFp\":\"d8fb7c652109e127a5a49468514240cbd2ec752984de6358791b5b146d1fe0cd\",\"subject\":\"01a1a342-aa84-7000-9ee8-490844dd03fd\",\"v\":1,\"which\":\"claude-code\",\"who\":\"mnid:7e28947e3855176749823c7369d156822babbed85462dcbc131e79de1a292a64\"},\"link\":{\"hash\":\"6f54b7122a09e87d370c730a864218e5b3827d27270c848b92f8fb805e69378e\",\"prev\":\"ef4e13b4acfe48e39dbd3ce415dc13b902100aab39dcd6dcd928a6b1a7f6019b\",\"seq\":3,\"tail\":\"d8fb7c652109e127a5a49468514240cbd2ec752984de6358791b5b146d1fe0cd-157343dc41b0d28d2dc5cf5f679aa669\"}}",
